# Results as records: JSON Lines of cppverify.diagnostic/2, ending with a
# cppverify.summary/1 record; one SARIF 2.1.0 log made of the same records;
# and, in GitHub mode, the text with a workflow annotation after each error and
# warning. The compiler's own diagnostics are records too. A record's source
# spans its expression, from its first column to the one after its last.
#
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --jobs=1 --diagnostics-format=json %S/Inputs/structured_output.cpp -- 2>/dev/null \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=JSON
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --jobs=1 --diagnostics-format=sarif %S/Inputs/structured_output.cpp -- 2>/dev/null \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SARIF
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --diagnostics-format=json %S/Inputs/structured_syntax_error.cpp -- 2>/dev/null \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FRONTEND
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --jobs=1 --obligation-out=%t.cpv %S/Inputs/structured_output.cpp -- > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --obligation-in=%t.cpv --diagnostics-format=sarif 2>/dev/null \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REPLAY
# RUN: cd %S/Inputs && not %cpp-verify --jobs=1 --diagnostics-format=github structured_output.cpp -- 2>/dev/null \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GITHUB

The compiler's warning comes first, with its notes as related locations.
JSON:      {"message":"using the result of an assignment as a condition without parentheses","option":"-Wparentheses","related":[{"message":"place parentheses around the assignment to silence this warning","source":{"column":9,"end_column":9,"end_line":26,"file":"{{.*}}structured_output.cpp","line":26}},{"message":"use '==' to turn this assignment into an equality comparison","source":{{.*}}}],"schema":"cppverify.diagnostic/2","severity":"warning","source":{"column":7,"end_column":12,"end_line":26,"file":"{{.*}}structured_output.cpp","line":26},"status":"frontend"}
Every result names its function and where it is declared.
JSON-NEXT: {"backend":"z3","function":"inc","function_source":{"column":5,"end_column":8,"end_line":3,"file":"{{.*}}structured_output.cpp","line":3},"message":"inc [backend=z3]","schema":"cppverify.diagnostic/2","severity":"note","status":"verified"}
A failure spans the expression it checks, and gives its counterexample and
the steps of its path as the text prints them.
JSON-NEXT: {"backend":"z3","counterexample":"x = {{-[0-9]+}}, result = {{-?[0-9]+}}","function":"clamp"
JSON-SAME: "obligation":{"id":"{{.*}}::postcondition@11:23","kind":"postcondition","source":{"column":12,"end_column":27,"end_line":11,"file":"{{.*}}structured_output.cpp","line":11}}
JSON-SAME: "source":{"column":12,"end_column":27,"end_line":11,"file":"{{.*}}structured_output.cpp","line":11},"status":"failed"
JSON-SAME: "text":"takes the true branch"
JSON-SAME: "text":"returns {{-?[0-9]+}}"
JSON-NEXT: "function":"never"{{.*}}"status":"verified","vacuous":true}
JSON-NEXT: {"function":"never","function_source":{"column":5,"end_column":10,"end_line":18,"file":"{{.*}}structured_output.cpp","line":18},"message":"never: the precondition is unsatisfiable, so every claim about it holds vacuously","schema":"cppverify.diagnostic/2","severity":"warning","status":"warning"}
The run ends with its counts.
JSON-NEXT: {"bounded_safe":0,"exported":0,"failed":1,"interrupted":0,"lowered":0,"reasons":{},"schema":"cppverify.summary/1","trusted":0,"unresolved":0,"verified":2}
JSON-NOT: {{.}}

