A compiler error is a record of its own, and nothing is verified.
FRONTEND:      {"message":"expected ';' after return statement","schema":"cppverify.diagnostic/2","severity":"error","source":{"column":11,"end_column":11,"end_line":4,"file":"{{.*}}structured_syntax_error.cpp","line":4},"status":"frontend"}
FRONTEND-NEXT: {{.*}}"failed":0,{{.*}}"schema":"cppverify.summary/1",{{.*}}"verified":0}

An archive keeps the range a failure spans.
REPLAY:      "kind": "fail",
REPLAY-NEXT: "level": "error",
REPLAY:      "endColumn": 27,
REPLAY-NEXT: "endLine": 11,
REPLAY-NEXT: "startColumn": 12,
REPLAY-NEXT: "startLine": 11
REPLAY:      "ruleId": "postcondition",

GitHub's annotations name files relative to the working directory.
GITHUB:      ::warning file=structured_output.cpp,line=26,col=7,endLine=26,endColumn=12,title=clang::using the result of an assignment as a condition without parentheses
GITHUB:      Verified: inc [backend=z3]
GITHUB:      ::error file=structured_output.cpp,line=11,col=12,endLine=11,endColumn=27,title=cpp-verify%3A postcondition::verification failed: clamp [postcondition] [backend=z3] [reason=counterexample]%0Acounterexample: x = {{-[0-9]+}}, result = {{-?[0-9]+}}
GITHUB:      ::warning file=structured_output.cpp,line=18,col=5,endLine=18,endColumn=10,title=cpp-verify::never: the precondition is unsatisfiable, so every claim about it holds vacuously
GITHUB:      Summary: 2 verified, 1 failed
